  "id": "greek_rock",
  "name": "Greek rock",
  "family": "rock_punk",
  "lineage": "Greek-language rock music developed from 1960s onward, integrating Greek-laiko and rebetiko folk-music influences with broader Western rock vocabulary. The 1960s Pavlos Sidiropoulos and Stamatis Spanoudakis era inaugurated the form; the 1980s-90s \"Greek rock\" wave through Magic de Spell, Trypes, Tripes, Pyx Lax, and the broader post-1981 Athens scene consolidated commercial visibility. Distinguished by Greek-language lyrics and frequent integration of bouzouki/baglamas folk-instruments into rock contexts.",
